{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To install the package, run the following command:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add -D @tanstack/publish-config","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To use the TanStack Config programmatically, you can import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"publish"},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { publish } from '@tanstack/publish-config'\n\npublish({\n  branchConfigs: configOpts.branchConfigs,\n  packages: configOpts.packages,\n  rootDir: configOpts.rootDir,\n  branch: process.env.BRANCH,\n  tag: process.env.TAG,\n  ghToken: process.env.GH_TOKEN,\n})\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('Successfully published packages!')\n  })\n  .catch(console.error)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The programmatic usage is only available for ESM packages. To support this, you have to have:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"type\": \"module\"\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":" file and use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"require"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"trusted-publishing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trusted Publishing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trusted publishing is the new npm strategy to allow publishing packages without npm tokens, using OIDC authentication. It currently requires you to set up for each package individually; however, once enabled, no further interaction is required!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 1"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the package already has a published version on npm, you can skip this step."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the package has never been published, you can publish a \"placeholder\" package to do the setup process. This CLI tool streamlines this: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/azu/setup-npm-trusted-publish","children":[{"type":"text","value":"setup-npm-trusted-publish"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 2"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you're only setting up one package, you can skip this step. Otherwise, the tools below help dramatically when setting up 5+ packages all at once."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/antfu/open-packages-on-npm","children":[{"type":"text","value":"open-packages-on-npm"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/sxzz/userscripts/blob/main/src/npm-trusted-publisher.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sxzz's userscript"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 3"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fill in the fields on the package's settings page, similar to this. You will need to authenticate with MFA to save these settings."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"image","src":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/config/main/heads/main/media/trusted-publisher.png","alt":"Settings"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"trusted-publishing","text":"Trusted Publishing","level":2},{"id":"step-1","text":"Step 1","level":3},{"id":"step-2","text":"Step 2","level":3},{"id":"step-3","text":"Step 3","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Installation\n\nTo install the package, run the following command:\n\n```bash\npnpm add -D @tanstack/publish-config\n```\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use the TanStack Config programmatically, you can import the `publish` function:\n\n```ts\nimport { publish } from '@tanstack/publish-config'\n\npublish({\n  branchConfigs: configOpts.branchConfigs,\n  packages: configOpts.packages,\n  rootDir: configOpts.rootDir,\n  branch: process.env.BRANCH,\n  tag: process.env.TAG,\n  ghToken: process.env.GH_TOKEN,\n})\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('Successfully published packages!')\n  })\n  .catch(console.error)\n```\n\n> The programmatic usage is only available for ESM packages. To support this, you have to have:\n>\n> ```json\n> {\n>   \"type\": \"module\"\n> }\n> ```\n>\n> in your `package.json` file and use `import` instead of `require`.\n\n## Trusted Publishing\n\nTrusted publishing is the new npm strategy to allow publishing packages without npm tokens, using OIDC authentication. It currently requires you to set up for each package individually; however, once enabled, no further interaction is required!\n\n### Step 1\n\n- If the package already has a published version on npm, you can skip this step.\n- If the package has never been published, you can publish a \"placeholder\" package to do the setup process. This CLI tool streamlines this: [setup-npm-trusted-publish](https://github.com/azu/setup-npm-trusted-publish)\n\n### Step 2\n\n- If you're only setting up one package, you can skip this step. Otherwise, the tools below help dramatically when setting up 5+ packages all at once.\n- [open-packages-on-npm](https://github.com/antfu/open-packages-on-npm)\n- [sxzz's userscript](https://github.com/sxzz/userscripts/blob/main/src/npm-trusted-publisher.md)\n\n### Step 3\n\n- Fill in the fields on the package's settings page, similar to this. You will need to authenticate with MFA to save these settings.\n\n![Settings](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/config/main/heads/main/media/trusted-publisher.png)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: publish\ntitle: Publish\n---\n\n## Installation\n\nTo install the package, run the following command:\n\n```bash\npnpm add -D @tanstack/publish-config\n```\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use the TanStack Config programmatically, you can import the `publish` function:\n\n```ts\nimport { publish } from '@tanstack/publish-config'\n\npublish({\n  branchConfigs: configOpts.branchConfigs,\n  packages: configOpts.packages,\n  rootDir: configOpts.rootDir,\n  branch: process.env.BRANCH,\n  tag: process.env.TAG,\n  ghToken: process.env.GH_TOKEN,\n})\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('Successfully published packages!')\n  })\n  .catch(console.error)\n```\n\n> The programmatic usage is only available for ESM packages. To support this, you have to have:\n>\n> ```json\n> {\n>   \"type\": \"module\"\n> }\n> ```\n>\n> in your `package.json` file and use `import` instead of `require`.\n\n## Trusted Publishing\n\nTrusted publishing is the new npm strategy to allow publishing packages without npm tokens, using OIDC authentication. It currently requires you to set up for each package individually; however, once enabled, no further interaction is required!\n\n### Step 1\n\n- If the package already has a published version on npm, you can skip this step.\n- If the package has never been published, you can publish a \"placeholder\" package to do the setup process. This CLI tool streamlines this: [setup-npm-trusted-publish](https://github.com/azu/setup-npm-trusted-publish)\n\n### Step 2\n\n- If you're only setting up one package, you can skip this step. Otherwise, the tools below help dramatically when setting up 5+ packages all at once.\n- [open-packages-on-npm](https://github.com/antfu/open-packages-on-npm)\n- [sxzz's userscript](https://github.com/sxzz/userscripts/blob/main/src/npm-trusted-publisher.md)\n\n### Step 3\n\n- Fill in the fields on the package's settings page, similar to this. You will need to authenticate with MFA to save these settings.\n\n![Settings](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/config/refs/heads/main/media/trusted-publisher.png)\n"}
